 See instructions in the [project's website](https://www.navidrome.org/docs/installation/)
 
+## Trusted reverse proxy login
+
+To let a reverse proxy authenticate browser users, set `ReverseProxyWhitelist` to
+the proxy's IP address or comma-separated IPv4/IPv6 CIDR ranges, and have the
+proxy send the authenticated username in `Remote-User`. Set
+`ReverseProxyUserHeader` if your proxy uses another header. For a Unix socket,
+use `@` in the whitelist. An empty whitelist disables this login method.
+
+Only whitelist addresses that belong to proxies which remove any incoming
+user header before setting their own. A broad range such as `0.0.0.0/0` lets
+clients claim any username, including an administrator's.
+
 ## Features
  
  - Handles very **large music collections**
